    <briefdescription>
<para>A Multi-Value Register. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Concurrent writes from different nodes both survive until one supersedes the other. Each write is tagged with a <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1crdt_1_1_dot" kindref="compound">Dot</ref>; a merge retains all values whose dot is not dominated by another node&apos;s vector clock.</para>
<para>For simplicity this implementation retains all concurrent values without vector-clock dominance pruning. Values are deduplicated on write.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Value type (must be equality-comparable and copy-constructible). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
